The one-time SAST adoption baseline has NOT been generated yet.

While this file exists, tools/ci/security-baseline.json is [] and the
local-ci/security leg fails closed, whatever the OpenGrep scan finds.

The baseline must come from one full scan of the tree under review, run once
on the CI server (a full scan exceeds the time a contributor workstation may
spend on one CI command):

    bun tools/ci/cli/sast-baseline.ts

from a clean checkout at the repository root. The command writes every
ERROR finding into tools/ci/security-baseline.json and deletes this file.
Then: triage each entry (fix real bugs, replace the reason with the triage),
set BASELINE_CEILING in tests/local-ci-baseline.test.mjs to the entry count,
and commit all three changes together. See ADR-0060 D4.
